1
00:00:01,534 --> 00:00:02,736
- Metz.
- Here.

2
00:00:03,269 --> 00:00:07,340
<i>By combining Internal Medicine and Surgery</i>

3
00:00:07,407 --> 00:00:10,944
to establish
the Medical Solutions Headquarters,

4
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:13,279
our hospital is starting over.

5
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:16,149
We will administer cutting-edge,
next-generation treatment

6
00:00:16,216 --> 00:00:18,485
led by Internal Medicine.

7
00:00:18,551 --> 00:00:22,522
Let us review what that means.

8
00:00:22,589 --> 00:00:24,357
CHOKO MIKUNI, PR CHIEF

9
00:00:25,558 --> 00:00:29,829
This is this week's surgery schedule
at our hospital.

10
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,065
It's packed with surgeries.

11
00:00:32,132 --> 00:00:34,334
Ordinarily,
we should be drastically reducing

12
00:00:34,401 --> 00:00:37,003
the number of old-fashioned surgeries.

13
00:00:38,438 --> 00:00:42,042
Can anyone explain what's happening here?

14
00:00:42,108 --> 00:00:42,942
Sure.

15
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:46,379
Until recently,

16
00:00:46,446 --> 00:00:48,214
in accordance with COVID protocols,

17
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:51,484
we've asked many patients
to postpone their surgeries.

18
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:55,155
<i>The other day, we started performing</i>
<i>the surgeries that were postponed.</i>

19
00:00:55,855 --> 00:01:00,260
<i>We are currently busy</i>
<i>with the most urgent of surgeries.</i>

20
00:01:00,326 --> 00:01:01,294
<i>Excuse me!</i>

21
00:01:01,361 --> 00:01:05,298
Operating on ordinary people
who carry no influence

22
00:01:05,365 --> 00:01:09,235
has absolutely zero benefits.

23
00:01:09,302 --> 00:01:10,937
- "Zero benefits"?
- Why you…

24
00:01:11,004 --> 00:01:13,573
Now, now! Cut that out!

25
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,308
Sit back down!

26
00:01:17,710 --> 00:01:23,550
Well now, the way I see things,
Chief Hachisuka, in my opinion--

27
00:01:23,616 --> 00:01:29,756
Allow me to remind you
of how our hospital operates.

28
00:01:29,823 --> 00:01:30,990
Right.

29
00:01:31,057 --> 00:01:34,327
As the effective head
of this hospital, I think--

30
00:01:34,394 --> 00:01:36,296
There are three main points!

31
00:01:36,362 --> 00:01:39,165
Oh, you'll put it on the screen?
That's nice.

32
00:01:39,232 --> 00:01:42,168
Acting Director Hiruma is being
completely left out.

33
00:01:42,235 --> 00:01:43,703
It makes me kind of sad.

34
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:44,604
Point one!

35
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:49,542
Establishment of futuristic
preventative medicine

36
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:52,545
through the creation
of the Infection Research Center.

37
00:01:52,612 --> 00:01:53,613
Point two.

38
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:57,417
The total reduction
of unnecessary surgeries.

39
00:01:57,484 --> 00:01:59,119
And point three!

40
00:01:59,185 --> 00:02:01,921
Intensification of PR activities!

41
00:02:04,691 --> 00:02:08,495
Now that Totei University Hospital
has been reborn,

42
00:02:08,561 --> 00:02:13,600
knowledge of it must be spread
and our influence must be increased.

43
00:02:13,666 --> 00:02:16,136
That is the most urgent matter.

44
00:02:16,703 --> 00:02:17,604
That's right.

45
00:02:18,171 --> 00:02:21,307
What's important is branding!

46
00:02:27,247 --> 00:02:28,148
Chief Hachisuka.

47
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,019
There's someone I would like to introduce.

48
00:02:33,586 --> 00:02:34,754
Come upfront, please.

49
00:02:38,224 --> 00:02:43,897
To support Totei University Hospital's
branding activities,

50
00:02:44,564 --> 00:02:47,534
I have brought in
this medical world influencer.

51
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:52,539
Dr. Morimoto!

52
00:02:58,111 --> 00:02:59,812
What happened to Dr. Morimoto?

53
00:02:59,879 --> 00:03:01,314
He looks ridiculous.

54
00:03:01,381 --> 00:03:05,285
- Is that the real Dr. Morimoto?
- Oh, wow! It's the real deal!

55
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:08,354
Hello, everyone. I'm Dr. Morimoto.

56
00:03:08,421 --> 00:03:11,157
He's so refined and cool now!

57
00:03:11,224 --> 00:03:13,393
- It's nice to have you.
- It's nice to be here.

58
00:03:15,395 --> 00:03:17,363
It feels like I'm being ignored.

59
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:23,803
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

60
00:03:25,138 --> 00:03:26,973
<i>2021.</i>

61
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:30,043
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

62
00:03:30,109 --> 00:03:33,146
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

63
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,014
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>

64
00:03:35,081 --> 00:03:37,116
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

65
00:03:37,183 --> 00:03:40,453
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

66
00:03:45,758 --> 00:03:47,393
Dr. Daimon.

67
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:48,795
It has been a while.

68
00:03:48,861 --> 00:03:52,665
You're as busy as ever.
I respect you very much for that.

69
00:03:53,166 --> 00:03:54,367
Your collar is funny.

70
00:03:56,736 --> 00:03:58,504
I can see you're surprised.

71
00:03:58,571 --> 00:03:59,706
I guess it makes sense.

72
00:04:00,306 --> 00:04:03,376
I've completely changed since then.

73
00:04:03,443 --> 00:04:06,446
How many years have you been a surgeon?
You're a failure!

74
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,414
<i>Please!</i>

75
00:04:08,481 --> 00:04:10,483
I want to save Shiori!

76
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:12,619
Then do it yourself.

77
00:04:13,419 --> 00:04:17,156
I'm no longer a hopeless doctor
who begs for your help.

78
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:20,493
I've obtained so much influence,

79
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,763
I could take over this hospital
if I wanted to.

80
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,733
Let me show you, Dr. Daimon, how much…

81
00:04:26,799 --> 00:04:27,634
She's gone.

82
00:04:31,671 --> 00:04:33,473
You'll soon see.

83
00:04:34,841 --> 00:04:35,675
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

84
00:04:35,742 --> 00:04:38,778
<i>this freelance maverick doctor</i>

85
00:04:38,845 --> 00:04:43,016
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

86
00:04:43,082 --> 00:04:44,617
What was his name again?

87
00:04:45,585 --> 00:04:47,754
SHICHIMIYA DINER

88
00:04:49,722 --> 00:04:51,624
- ExTuber?
- That's right.

89
00:04:51,691 --> 00:04:54,694
Dr. Hikaru Morimoto is a name
from the distant past.

90
00:04:54,761 --> 00:04:57,230
Now, he's extremely successful.

91
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:58,131
Look at this.

92
00:04:59,399 --> 00:05:03,770
<i>It's Dr. Morimoto's Superpowered Channel!</i>

93
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,406
<i>I'm Dr. Morimoto!</i>

94
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:11,144
<i>Today, I'll tell you the worst three</i>
<i>food combinations ever!</i>

95
00:05:11,210 --> 00:05:12,712
How idiotic!

96
00:05:12,779 --> 00:05:16,783
He's a medical ExTuber
with over 500,000 followers.

97
00:05:16,849 --> 00:05:19,452
After gaining popularity
with young people,

98
00:05:19,519 --> 00:05:22,622
- he has now gained even wider appeal.
- Really?

99
00:05:22,689 --> 00:05:25,358
- Here's the minced meat cutlet set.
- This looks delicious!

100
00:05:25,858 --> 00:05:28,194
Lately, you haven't been cooking
for me at all, Akira.

101
00:05:28,261 --> 00:05:29,662
I told you, I'm busy.

102
00:05:29,729 --> 00:05:31,230
That sounds fishy.

103
00:05:31,297 --> 00:05:34,867
Hey, are you guys
friends with Dr. Morimoto?

104
00:05:34,934 --> 00:05:38,871
I'm a big fan!
Can you get his autograph for me?

105
00:05:38,938 --> 00:05:40,373
Oh, Mom! I'm sorry about her.

106
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:43,142
At first, I only peeked at him
when my daughter watched.

107
00:05:43,209 --> 00:05:46,979
But he's so instructive and funny.
And he's handsome too!

108
00:05:47,046 --> 00:05:49,449
Ma'am, this minced meat cutlet
is delicious!

109
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:52,452
- Are you even listening?
- It's really good.

110
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:56,856
- Are you okay, ma'am?
- Mom?

111
00:05:56,923 --> 00:05:58,324
- It's nothing.
- Are you okay?

112
00:05:58,391 --> 00:06:00,093
Here, let me feel it.

113
00:06:02,161 --> 00:06:04,430
I told you, it's nothing! Don't overreact!

114
00:06:04,931 --> 00:06:07,667
Mom, how many times
have I told you to see a doctor?

115
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:09,535
I'm just fine.

116
00:06:09,602 --> 00:06:12,438
Ma'am, let's run some tests.

117
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:17,410
<i>Voila! Dang! Look at that!</i>

118
00:06:17,477 --> 00:06:21,414
<i>It's a Niagara Falls of caramel sauce.</i>

119
00:06:21,481 --> 00:06:24,584
What's so interesting about this?

120
00:06:24,650 --> 00:06:28,988
He's just using kids' toys
to gain influence.

121
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:30,256
<i>It's so sweet.</i>

122
00:06:30,323 --> 00:06:32,258
Why the heck is he eating pudding?

123
00:06:32,325 --> 00:06:36,362
Yui, has my visitor arrived yet?

124
00:06:36,429 --> 00:06:38,064
Yes. He's downstairs.

125
00:06:38,131 --> 00:06:40,833
What? Why didn't you tell me sooner?

126
00:06:43,369 --> 00:06:47,573
<i>She hates groups,</i>

127
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,041
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

128
00:06:49,108 --> 00:06:50,543
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

129
00:06:51,344 --> 00:06:54,647
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

130
00:06:54,714 --> 00:06:56,449
<i>to work her way up.</i>

131
00:06:57,316 --> 00:07:00,019
- Yes, come in.
- Excuse me.

132
00:07:01,721 --> 00:07:05,191
- Well, well! Dr. Hiruma!
- Hello.

133
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:08,261
Thank you for coming,
Environment Minister Enomoto.

134
00:07:08,327 --> 00:07:09,429
I am Director Hiruma.

135
00:07:09,495 --> 00:07:15,067
You see, I will be indebted to you.
That's how I feel about being here.

136
00:07:16,068 --> 00:07:20,139
Just like on live parliamentary
broadcasts. What a nice voice!

137
00:07:20,206 --> 00:07:22,175
- Such flattery.
- Not at all.

138
00:07:22,241 --> 00:07:24,977
- I look forward to this.
- Me too.

139
00:07:25,545 --> 00:07:27,814
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

140
00:07:30,016 --> 00:07:33,686
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

141
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:05,184
Excuse me.

142
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:08,187
- Ma'am.
- Yes?

143
00:08:08,688 --> 00:08:10,990
Stomach cancer, stage 3.

144
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:12,525
Oh, dear!

145
00:08:12,592 --> 00:08:14,894
You should have gotten tested sooner.

146
00:08:14,961 --> 00:08:16,662
With the way things are, how can I?

147
00:08:16,729 --> 00:08:19,465
It's rough for hospital workers right now.

148
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:22,101
I thought I should hang tough
and soldier on.

149
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:24,070
We operate tomorrow, so you're staying.

150
00:08:24,136 --> 00:08:26,739
I can't do that!
I have a restaurant to run!

151
00:08:26,806 --> 00:08:28,107
- Now, listen.
- What?

152
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:30,610
Excuse me. Yasue Shichimiya,

153
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:34,447
I need to tell you something about
the surgery that Dr. Daimon mentioned.

154
00:08:35,348 --> 00:08:37,450
I'm afraid it must be postponed.

155
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:38,918
How come?

156
00:08:38,985 --> 00:08:42,221
As you know, medical facilities
have been crowded,

157
00:08:42,288 --> 00:08:44,423
so surgeries have been put on hold.

158
00:08:44,490 --> 00:08:45,791
What are you talking about?

159
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:48,094
You just said the OR was free tomorrow!

160
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,495
Things have changed!

161
00:08:49,562 --> 00:08:52,431
- So what?
- An emergency patient just arrived.

162
00:08:52,498 --> 00:08:54,100
Really?

163
00:08:56,469 --> 00:09:00,840
Thank you very much
for deciding to get surgery.

164
00:09:00,907 --> 00:09:02,542
You see,

165
00:09:03,109 --> 00:09:06,746
I knew that I couldn't allow this
to go on any longer.

166
00:09:06,812 --> 00:09:07,880
I appreciate this.

167
00:09:07,947 --> 00:09:08,814
Oh, well.

168
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:10,449
You see,

169
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:14,287
- I saw it in my mind.
- Yes?

170
00:09:14,353 --> 00:09:16,255
Really? What did you see?

171
00:09:16,322 --> 00:09:18,291
"Ope"!

172
00:09:18,357 --> 00:09:19,959
- Those letters!
- I see.

173
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:25,231
I thought it might be short for "opera."

174
00:09:25,298 --> 00:09:27,600
But it was for "operation."

175
00:09:27,667 --> 00:09:29,769
- Such a great talent for humor!
- Not at all!

176
00:09:29,835 --> 00:09:32,471
- Magnificent, isn't it?
- Yes, it is!

177
00:09:32,538 --> 00:09:34,574
Incidentally, Minister Enomoto,

178
00:09:35,308 --> 00:09:39,312
when your surgery
is successfully completed,

179
00:09:39,378 --> 00:09:41,147
you mentioned

180
00:09:41,213 --> 00:09:46,085
that you would grant our hospital
Green Ecology certification.

181
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:52,258
Well, that isn't why I asked you
to have your surgery here, however.

182
00:09:53,492 --> 00:09:55,628
You know, this hospital

183
00:09:55,695 --> 00:09:59,465
has paid a lot of consideration
to environmental concerns.

184
00:09:59,532 --> 00:10:02,501
I can see that there are lots
of plants too.

185
00:10:02,568 --> 00:10:05,605
As Environment Minister,

186
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:08,307
I believe I can…

187
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:11,010
be of assistance.

188
00:10:11,077 --> 00:10:13,312
Thank you so much.

189
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:15,147
Hey!

190
00:10:15,915 --> 00:10:17,883
Why was he urgently hospitalized?

191
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:20,052
- Hey, you! How rude!
- What?

192
00:10:20,119 --> 00:10:22,254
You part-timer, Michiko Daimon, get out.

193
00:10:22,321 --> 00:10:24,390
You took my OR!

194
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:26,659
- How dare you!
- Excuse me! Dr. Daimon!

195
00:10:26,726 --> 00:10:28,628
How dare you enter the minister's room!

196
00:10:28,694 --> 00:10:31,130
I'm terribly sorry
for the interruption. Let's go.

197
00:10:31,197 --> 00:10:35,034
- What? You're a minister?
- Shut up and get going! Go!

198
00:10:35,101 --> 00:10:37,269
I am terribly sorry.

199
00:10:38,170 --> 00:10:40,840
<i>Today, we have learned</i>

200
00:10:40,906 --> 00:10:44,477
<i>that Environment Minister Enomoto</i>
<i>has been urgently hospitalized.</i>

201
00:10:44,977 --> 00:10:48,981
<i>It's not clear what his illness might be.</i>

202
00:10:49,048 --> 00:10:50,449
<i>Just ahead of the Tokyo…</i>

203
00:10:50,516 --> 00:10:53,319
This is Acting Director Hiruma's doing.
How dare he.

204
00:10:53,886 --> 00:10:55,688
I'll find out what's up.

205
00:11:05,431 --> 00:11:09,335
He sure does behave without restraint.

206
00:11:13,506 --> 00:11:14,740
What? Where is she?

207
00:11:14,807 --> 00:11:17,276
- Where did this patient go?
- She was released.

208
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:18,644
What?

209
00:11:19,145 --> 00:11:20,146
SHICHIMIYA DINER

210
00:11:20,212 --> 00:11:22,481
- Here.
- Thank you!

211
00:11:22,548 --> 00:11:24,150
Ma'am. More rice, please.

212
00:11:24,216 --> 00:11:25,451
Sure thing.

213
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:27,620
Thank goodness, you're all right.

214
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:29,755
My daughter was just overreacting.

215
00:11:29,822 --> 00:11:31,157
Want seconds yet?

216
00:11:32,491 --> 00:11:34,660
Welcome! Oh, you.

217
00:11:34,727 --> 00:11:36,529
Don't act like that!

218
00:11:36,595 --> 00:11:38,230
Who said you could leave?

219
00:11:38,297 --> 00:11:41,500
I don't have the money
for a long hospital stay.

220
00:11:41,567 --> 00:11:44,070
Besides, they'll call
when my surgery is scheduled.

221
00:11:44,136 --> 00:11:46,605
That's just going to postpone it longer!

222
00:11:46,672 --> 00:11:48,574
- I saw the news.
- What?

223
00:11:48,641 --> 00:11:52,311
Naturally, a government minister
who works for the people is prioritized.

224
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:54,613
Important people like him should go first.

225
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:56,182
I can have mine later.

226
00:11:56,248 --> 00:11:57,717
- But you know--
- What?

227
00:11:57,783 --> 00:12:00,586
Will I die if I don't get surgery
today or tomorrow?

228
00:12:00,653 --> 00:12:02,254
You will if you ignore it!

229
00:12:02,321 --> 00:12:03,389
I'll be just fine.

230
00:12:03,456 --> 00:12:05,691
- Hang tough and soldier on.
- What?

231
00:12:05,758 --> 00:12:08,627
Dr. Morimoto is about to livestream!
If you're done, then leave!

232
00:12:08,694 --> 00:12:10,429
- Hey!
- Wait a second.

233
00:12:10,496 --> 00:12:12,364
You want something to eat?

234
00:12:12,431 --> 00:12:14,033
Ma'am, where are my seconds?

235
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:17,002
Oh, I'm sorry it's taking so long.

236
00:12:17,503 --> 00:12:20,439
As you can see, I'm superpowered!

237
00:12:20,506 --> 00:12:22,041
What is with that?

238
00:12:23,342 --> 00:12:27,813
It's Dr. Morimoto's Superpowered Channel!

239
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:30,015
Thank you.

240
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:33,185
Today, we're having a special livestream!

241
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:35,721
I'll be speaking with
Totei University Hospital's

242
00:12:35,788 --> 00:12:37,490
Medical Solutions Headquarters Chief,

243
00:12:37,556 --> 00:12:40,159
Dr. Hachisuka,
about next-generation medical care.

244
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:43,028
<i>Here at Totei University Hospital,</i>

245
00:12:43,095 --> 00:12:46,365
<i>you're treating patients</i>
<i>with cutting-edge medical treatments.</i>

246
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:50,069
<i>That's right. First, with the use</i>
<i>of online appointments…</i>

247
00:12:50,136 --> 00:12:52,772
Oh, wow! It says 20,000 people
are watching!

248
00:12:52,838 --> 00:12:55,908
Using a popular ExTuber
to promote the hospital

249
00:12:55,975 --> 00:12:58,778
is really a cutting-edge idea
from Chief Hachisuka.

250
00:12:59,645 --> 00:13:02,748
Dr. Morimoto is like a guru
among young doctors.

251
00:13:02,815 --> 00:13:04,250
Is that right?

252
00:13:04,984 --> 00:13:06,318
Have a look at this.

253
00:13:06,385 --> 00:13:09,455
This video has been watched
over a million times.

254
00:13:09,522 --> 00:13:11,590
<i>I bought a new motorcycle!</i>

255
00:13:11,657 --> 00:13:13,292
"I bought a new motorcycle"?

256
00:13:13,359 --> 00:13:15,027
What does this have to do with medicine?

257
00:13:15,528 --> 00:13:18,631
And his morning routine video
has been watched 400,000 times.

258
00:13:18,697 --> 00:13:21,534
<i>It's Dr. Morimoto's Morning Routine!</i>

259
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:23,002
<i>Okay, here we go!</i>

260
00:13:23,068 --> 00:13:25,504
<i>- I'm having steak!</i>
- Isn't this great?

261
00:13:25,571 --> 00:13:29,542
What? Are you guys impressed
by some ExTuber?

262
00:13:29,608 --> 00:13:32,411
But you're not impressed
by a super doctor like me?

263
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,612
- That's right.
- That's right.

264
00:13:34,113 --> 00:13:36,182
He makes a fortune too.

265
00:13:36,248 --> 00:13:38,284
With the number of views he gets,

266
00:13:38,350 --> 00:13:40,820
he probably makes hundreds of millions.

267
00:13:40,886 --> 00:13:43,122
- Hundreds of millions?
- It gives you hope!

268
00:13:43,189 --> 00:13:45,090
He's a hotshot ExTuber, after all.

269
00:13:45,157 --> 00:13:48,427
- This is making me sick.
- I can't take this!

270
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:52,198
While Dr. Morimoto is making
hundreds of millions with videos,

271
00:13:52,264 --> 00:13:54,667
we're operating like mad for a low salary!

272
00:13:54,733 --> 00:13:55,568
Now I'm ticked off.

273
00:13:55,634 --> 00:13:58,537
<i>We're taking this opportunity to start</i>

274
00:13:58,604 --> 00:14:01,507
<i>the Totei University Hospital</i>
<i>official channel.</i>

275
00:14:01,574 --> 00:14:04,043
<i>- What incredible news!</i>
- Give me a break.

276
00:14:04,109 --> 00:14:06,779
"Official channel"? Don't be ridiculous.

277
00:14:07,446 --> 00:14:10,683
Damn that Hachisuka
for doing whatever he likes…

278
00:14:10,749 --> 00:14:11,617
without my permission.

279
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:14,086
Damn that Hachisuka!

280
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:17,957
Just watch.

281
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:21,861
Once the minister's surgery
is completed tomorrow,

282
00:14:21,927 --> 00:14:24,597
the power structure at this hospital
will change entirely.

283
00:14:24,663 --> 00:14:27,399
- By the way…
- Yes?

284
00:14:27,466 --> 00:14:31,203
The reasons for the minister's
hospitalization are very top-secret.

285
00:14:31,270 --> 00:14:34,440
Make absolutely certain
nothing about it gets leaked.

286
00:14:34,506 --> 00:14:35,841
- Understood, sir.
- Good.

287
00:14:35,908 --> 00:14:38,677
- Superpowered!
- Superpowered!

288
00:14:39,478 --> 00:14:41,146
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

289
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:43,482
- Thank you!
- Keep up the good work!

290
00:14:45,951 --> 00:14:47,219
Dr. Daimon!

291
00:14:49,188 --> 00:14:50,289
Dr. Daimon!

292
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:53,225
What do you think?

293
00:14:53,292 --> 00:14:56,495
This is how I do my duty as a doctor now.

294
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,898
By the way,
why don't you appear on my channel?

295
00:14:58,964 --> 00:15:01,400
I won't! I don't need
a medical license for that.

296
00:15:01,967 --> 00:15:04,870
You know, Dr. Daimon,
your way of thinking is old-fashioned.

297
00:15:05,771 --> 00:15:06,906
"Old-fashioned"?

298
00:15:06,972 --> 00:15:09,742
A doctor can only save
so many people with surgery.

299
00:15:09,808 --> 00:15:12,645
But if you spread information
to lots of people like I do,

300
00:15:13,279 --> 00:15:16,615
tens of thousands of people
can be saved by that information.

301
00:15:17,716 --> 00:15:21,186
In the future,
a doctor's weapon won't be the scalpel.

302
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:23,789
- It will be influence!
- That makes no sense.

303
00:15:24,456 --> 00:15:25,457
What?

304
00:15:25,524 --> 00:15:27,993
Well, it's clear
you can't understand that.

305
00:15:28,494 --> 00:15:30,429
But I am a next-generation doctor.

306
00:15:30,496 --> 00:15:33,399
- That's so shallow.
- You're Dr. Morimoto, aren't you?

307
00:15:33,465 --> 00:15:38,037
See? My fans just can't help
chasing after me.

308
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:40,205
That's scary.

309
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:41,407
Because of you…

310
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,676
Because of you, my mother…

311
00:15:43,742 --> 00:15:45,511
What? What is it?

312
00:15:47,179 --> 00:15:48,180
<i>Everyone,</i>

313
00:15:48,247 --> 00:15:51,216
<i>medical facilities</i>
<i>are overwhelmed right now.</i>

314
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:55,120
<i>So let's avoid going to the hospital</i>
<i>if it's not an emergency.</i>

315
00:15:55,988 --> 00:15:59,425
<i>If your stomach hurts a little,</i>
<i>wait and see how it goes.</i>

316
00:15:59,491 --> 00:16:02,194
<i>Now is the time to hang tough</i>
<i>and soldier on.</i>

317
00:16:04,063 --> 00:16:05,597
After she saw this,

318
00:16:05,664 --> 00:16:08,467
my mom decided not to go to the hospital!

319
00:16:09,435 --> 00:16:10,736
But this…

320
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:14,807
<i>My mom has always been the type</i>
<i>who puts her needs after others.</i>

321
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,345
Hang tough and soldier on.

322
00:16:19,912 --> 00:16:22,414
She's a huge fan of yours,
so if you say this,

323
00:16:22,948 --> 00:16:24,783
of course, she's going to hang tough!

324
00:16:27,186 --> 00:16:29,188
If something happens to my mom,

325
00:16:30,122 --> 00:16:33,625
I will never forgive you!

326
00:16:40,466 --> 00:16:42,501
Influence is your weapon?

327
00:16:43,268 --> 00:16:44,803
That weapon is…

328
00:16:45,571 --> 00:16:47,172
killing people.

329
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,119
Chief Hachisuka,

330
00:17:00,185 --> 00:17:03,489
I have obtained info on
Environment Minister Enomoto's condition.

331
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:10,262
Oh, dear…

332
00:17:19,605 --> 00:17:22,307
Sorry, we're not open for dinner yet.

333
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:27,312
This is unbelievable.

334
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:30,716
I never thought I would meet Dr. Morimoto.

335
00:17:31,483 --> 00:17:33,719
I guess getting sick isn't all bad.

336
00:17:38,023 --> 00:17:41,493
I'm very sorry that my careless remarks

337
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:44,596
caused your disease to go undetected.

338
00:17:44,663 --> 00:17:47,766
I'll make sure your surgery
is scheduled right away.

339
00:17:47,833 --> 00:17:50,936
No, it's all right.
It isn't your fault. Have a seat.

340
00:17:52,938 --> 00:17:57,109
I know best what's happening with my body.

341
00:17:57,643 --> 00:18:01,513
I've always known
it's a very serious disease.

342
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,315
Then why didn't you…

343
00:18:05,350 --> 00:18:06,585
This restaurant,

344
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:09,321
I took it over after my husband.

345
00:18:09,388 --> 00:18:11,824
Since then, my daughter and I have run it.

346
00:18:12,391 --> 00:18:14,193
Due to COVID…

347
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,663
we've been quite in a difficult situation.

348
00:18:18,664 --> 00:18:21,333
Since we can't serve liquor,

349
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,602
sales have really declined.

350
00:18:25,137 --> 00:18:26,738
We lost a lot of customers.

351
00:18:27,673 --> 00:18:29,608
And that government compensation…

352
00:18:30,242 --> 00:18:32,511
They said our paperwork was incomplete,

353
00:18:33,178 --> 00:18:34,746
so we never got any.

354
00:18:38,350 --> 00:18:39,585
We're closing this place.

355
00:18:43,922 --> 00:18:45,457
So…

356
00:18:46,592 --> 00:18:48,360
I'm ashamed to say this…

357
00:18:49,328 --> 00:18:52,331
but if my daughter can get
my life insurance money,

358
00:18:52,831 --> 00:18:57,836
things might be a little better for her.

359
00:18:59,638 --> 00:19:00,639
That's why.

360
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:02,674
You're kidding.

361
00:19:03,208 --> 00:19:06,311
You can't do that!
You have to get surgery!

362
00:19:06,378 --> 00:19:08,280
You can't give up hope!

363
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:13,385
You are really a kind doctor, aren't you?

364
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:18,490
No, I'm not.

365
00:19:19,358 --> 00:19:20,759
I'm…

366
00:19:22,361 --> 00:19:23,562
I'm…

367
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:29,168
Yasue?

368
00:19:30,302 --> 00:19:31,336
Yasue!

369
00:19:31,403 --> 00:19:33,305
Yasue, are you all right?

370
00:19:33,372 --> 00:19:35,974
- Mom!
- Yasue!

371
00:19:36,041 --> 00:19:37,543
Call an ambulance!

372
00:19:38,143 --> 00:19:40,345
Yasue, can you hear me?

373
00:19:44,983 --> 00:19:47,119
The ulcer floor is hemorrhaging.

374
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,254
She's stabilized now,

375
00:19:49,321 --> 00:19:51,456
but if that metastasizes,
it will be too late.

376
00:19:51,523 --> 00:19:53,392
Her surgery can't be put off any longer.

377
00:19:54,259 --> 00:19:57,696
But she says she won't undergo surgery.

378
00:19:57,763 --> 00:19:58,864
What?

379
00:19:58,931 --> 00:20:01,433
She's refusing to be operated on.

380
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,302
Besides, the ORs are full.

381
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:04,636
There's nothing we can do.

382
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:06,572
Then go and convince her.

383
00:20:07,072 --> 00:20:09,107
Your influence is your weapon, right?

384
00:20:09,174 --> 00:20:10,742
But…

385
00:20:10,809 --> 00:20:13,278
Your influence is your weapon, right?

386
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:30,495
There's no way I can do it.

387
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:33,699
You couldn't convince her, huh?

388
00:20:34,299 --> 00:20:36,068
SURGERY CONSENT FORM

389
00:20:36,134 --> 00:20:38,170
The truth is…

390
00:20:39,338 --> 00:20:41,607
I'm a useless doctor

391
00:20:41,673 --> 00:20:45,310
that nobody needs at all!

392
00:20:46,878 --> 00:20:49,615
<i>Before I knew it,</i>
<i>I was talking about myself,</i>

393
00:20:49,681 --> 00:20:51,650
<i>and crying so hard, it was shocking.</i>

394
00:20:52,651 --> 00:20:54,219
I'm sorry!

395
00:20:56,255 --> 00:21:01,526
I'm not such a great person
that I'm able to influence people.

396
00:21:01,593 --> 00:21:04,396
- Yes, I know.
- Sorry, pal.

397
00:21:04,463 --> 00:21:06,198
I would like to cheer you up,

398
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:10,068
but the thought that you make a fortune
prevents me from doing it.

399
00:21:10,135 --> 00:21:12,537
- I don't feel like cheering you up.
- I know how you feel.

400
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:13,438
Really?

401
00:21:13,505 --> 00:21:14,606
You see…

402
00:21:15,173 --> 00:21:17,609
I can't be friends with some damn ExTuber.

403
00:21:19,711 --> 00:21:21,046
I can understand that.

404
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:24,082
Don't talk like that.
I'll take care of the bill here.

405
00:21:24,149 --> 00:21:25,784
You know, there's a part of me…

406
00:21:25,851 --> 00:21:29,755
that thinks, "You millionaire,
you damn well better pay the bill!"

407
00:21:29,821 --> 00:21:32,224
We should have gone somewhere
more expensive.

408
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:34,293
Yes. We always come to this place.

409
00:21:34,359 --> 00:21:35,360
To be honest,

410
00:21:35,427 --> 00:21:37,696
I'm always just running away.

411
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:40,832
These last few years,
I helped at my father's clinic,

412
00:21:40,899 --> 00:21:43,302
but COVID made business difficult.

413
00:21:43,368 --> 00:21:46,638
I tried to figure out a way
to make money for a while

414
00:21:46,705 --> 00:21:48,607
and started doing ExTube videos.

415
00:21:48,674 --> 00:21:51,743
HARD ABS IN JUST ONE WEEK
SURGEON, HIKARU MORIMOTO (38)

416
00:21:56,715 --> 00:21:59,918
<i>Then my video just happened to go viral.</i>

417
00:22:01,053 --> 00:22:02,054
Inside,

418
00:22:02,587 --> 00:22:03,822
I was relieved…

419
00:22:05,924 --> 00:22:09,261
I could escape
from being a useless doctor.

420
00:22:10,862 --> 00:22:11,863
But

421
00:22:12,631 --> 00:22:14,433
it has been harsh

422
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:16,601
since I feel so guilty.

423
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:19,838
What do you expect from me
when you whimper like that?

424
00:22:19,905 --> 00:22:21,873
What? You're crying?

425
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:23,709
What part made you cry?

426
00:22:23,775 --> 00:22:25,544
Dr. Morimoto…

427
00:22:26,378 --> 00:22:28,747
- You've been through a lot.
- Yes.

428
00:22:28,814 --> 00:22:30,749
You sure cry easily.

429
00:22:30,816 --> 00:22:35,620
You know what I think?
Ultimately, us humans…

430
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:40,125
We've simply got to fight
with the weapons we've been given.

431
00:22:41,626 --> 00:22:44,363
By the way…

432
00:22:45,263 --> 00:22:47,432
What is my weapon?

433
00:22:48,133 --> 00:22:49,167
That would be…

434
00:22:51,603 --> 00:22:54,473
- You know, right, Dr. Kaji?
- Yes…

435
00:22:56,108 --> 00:22:57,576
Forget it!

436
00:22:57,642 --> 00:23:00,212
I know you think I'm useless!

437
00:23:01,179 --> 00:23:05,684
Over 10,000 subscribers just today alone?

438
00:23:05,751 --> 00:23:08,153
You're really something, Chief Hachisuka.

439
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,155
This is what branding is all about.

440
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:13,191
It will become great PR
for the Totei University Hospital brand.

441
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:16,027
But you know…

442
00:23:17,763 --> 00:23:23,034
this kind of thing is nothing more
than silly videos for children.

443
00:23:23,101 --> 00:23:27,005
You shouldn't underestimate
the power of videos nowadays.

444
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:29,941
You know, if tomorrow's surgery…

445
00:23:30,776 --> 00:23:34,880
on Environment Minister Enomoto goes well,

446
00:23:35,447 --> 00:23:39,418
our hospital will apparently be granted

447
00:23:39,484 --> 00:23:43,121
Green Ecology certification.

448
00:23:44,556 --> 00:23:46,358
When that happens,

449
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:48,427
we'll become one

450
00:23:48,493 --> 00:23:50,262
of the leading hospitals in Japan.

451
00:23:50,328 --> 00:23:54,599
Don't you think
that's what real branding is?

452
00:23:57,135 --> 00:24:01,440
Is Minister Enomoto's illness
quite serious?

453
00:24:01,506 --> 00:24:03,708
No. It's nothing really.

454
00:24:05,076 --> 00:24:09,681
At the hands of our Surgery Department,
it's nothing at all.

455
00:24:09,748 --> 00:24:12,417
You're really something,
Acting Director Hiruma.

456
00:24:12,484 --> 00:24:15,120
Another job that's worthy
of your position.

457
00:24:20,025 --> 00:24:21,860
<i>Michiko! There's big trouble!</i>

458
00:24:21,927 --> 00:24:24,429
Get out here now! Right now!

459
00:24:26,531 --> 00:24:30,368
Damn it! Why are you
waking me up so early, Akira?

460
00:24:30,435 --> 00:24:33,905
Cut that out! Get over here
and watch this! Get over here!

461
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:36,842
- Quit making such noise!
- Watch! This is it!

462
00:24:36,908 --> 00:24:39,778
<i>We've learned more about</i>
<i>Environment Minister Enomoto</i>

463
00:24:39,845 --> 00:24:42,914
<i>who was urgently admitted</i>
<i>to the hospital yesterday.</i>

464
00:24:42,981 --> 00:24:46,117
<i>The information we have</i>
<i>is that he has paranasal sinusitis.</i>

465
00:24:46,751 --> 00:24:48,353
"Paranasal sinusitis"?

466
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:51,189
Apparently, his symptoms are quite mild.

467
00:24:51,256 --> 00:24:53,091
He just gets a runny nose sometimes.

468
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:58,730
<i>If this is true,</i>

469
00:24:58,797 --> 00:25:02,567
<i>he is sure to be criticized</i>
<i>for being hospitalized now</i>

470
00:25:02,634 --> 00:25:04,836
<i>just before the summit on the environment.</i>

471
00:25:04,903 --> 00:25:07,873
I wonder who leaked this information.

472
00:25:07,939 --> 00:25:10,876
<i>Vice Minister Hanaoka is scheduled</i>
<i>to appear instead,</i>

473
00:25:10,942 --> 00:25:13,311
<i>and he is preparing for the summit…</i>

474
00:25:14,346 --> 00:25:16,848
- Acting Director Hiruma!
- Acting Director Hiruma!

475
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:19,818
We heard that Environment Minister Enomoto

476
00:25:19,885 --> 00:25:22,087
only has mild paranasal sinusitis.

477
00:25:22,153 --> 00:25:23,455
If that's true,

478
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:26,525
this could be viewed
as dodging the summit!

479
00:25:27,225 --> 00:25:33,198
Environment Minister Enomoto
has a very serious illness

480
00:25:33,265 --> 00:25:36,768
and he must undergo emergency surgery.

481
00:25:36,835 --> 00:25:39,404
<i>That is why he was hospitalized.</i>

482
00:25:39,471 --> 00:25:40,972
<i>As you have just seen,</i>

483
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:42,774
<i>a hospital executive has stated</i>

484
00:25:42,841 --> 00:25:45,877
that Environment Minister Enomoto
has a serious illness.

485
00:25:46,978 --> 00:25:49,381
Don't you think this is a big problem too?

486
00:25:49,447 --> 00:25:52,350
Yes, it has become a bit of an issue.

487
00:25:52,417 --> 00:25:53,718
Now that there are reports

488
00:25:53,785 --> 00:25:58,189
that he's gravely ill, we can't say
he has mild paranasal sinusitis.

489
00:25:58,256 --> 00:25:59,591
- You!
- Yes, sir!

490
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:04,396
If we announced the truth now,
it would cause an uproar!

491
00:26:04,462 --> 00:26:07,299
No matter what we do, we're ruined!

492
00:26:07,365 --> 00:26:08,700
Yes?

493
00:26:09,634 --> 00:26:11,303
- What's going on here?
- What?

494
00:26:11,369 --> 00:26:14,272
I'll finish that sinusitis quickly,
so let me operate on that woman!

495
00:26:14,339 --> 00:26:16,274
We're dealing with a complex problem now.

496
00:26:16,341 --> 00:26:19,678
Who cares what happens
to some ordinary person!

497
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:22,647
The future of our country is at risk here!

498
00:26:22,714 --> 00:26:24,482
"Ordinary person"?

499
00:26:25,050 --> 00:26:26,618
Then who the heck is he?

500
00:26:26,685 --> 00:26:29,354
I am a government minister!

501
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:31,222
What a moron.

502
00:26:31,289 --> 00:26:32,691
That's not fair!

503
00:26:32,757 --> 00:26:36,561
You asked him what he was,
and he told you about it!

504
00:26:36,628 --> 00:26:38,263
A person's life is at risk here!

505
00:26:38,330 --> 00:26:39,631
Lately,

506
00:26:39,698 --> 00:26:42,400
a lot more people tell me
that they can't understand me

507
00:26:42,467 --> 00:26:45,670
because my nose sounds stuffed up.

508
00:26:45,737 --> 00:26:49,574
It's something that puts
the life of a politician at risk.

509
00:26:49,641 --> 00:26:52,243
That makes no sense at all. That's absurd.

510
00:26:52,310 --> 00:26:55,180
Yes, my English is absurdly good.

511
00:26:56,881 --> 00:26:58,516
I'll operate on the lady first.

512
00:26:58,583 --> 00:26:59,951
Wait! Hold on a second!

513
00:27:00,018 --> 00:27:01,886
- Wait!
- Settle down!

514
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:09,694
Please allow me to provide

515
00:27:09,761 --> 00:27:13,565
a solution to all these problems at once.

516
00:27:17,502 --> 00:27:20,038
Three. Two.

517
00:27:21,439 --> 00:27:26,211
Welcome, viewers of Totei University
Hospital's official channel.

518
00:27:26,277 --> 00:27:31,650
<i>Today, I will explain the disease</i>

519
00:27:31,716 --> 00:27:33,718
<i>that Environment Minister Enomoto has.</i>

520
00:27:35,153 --> 00:27:40,291
<i>Environment Minister Enomoto</i>
<i>has stage 3 stomach cancer.</i>

521
00:27:40,358 --> 00:27:41,259
It's true!

522
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:42,927
He is seriously ill.

523
00:27:42,994 --> 00:27:46,197
<i>His surgery is extremely complicated.</i>

524
00:27:46,264 --> 00:27:49,734
<i>Due to Minister Enomoto's</i>
<i>strong desire to…</i>

525
00:27:49,801 --> 00:27:54,239
<i>contribute to the future development</i>
<i>of medicine,</i>

526
00:27:54,305 --> 00:27:59,544
Minister Enomoto's emergency surgery

527
00:27:59,611 --> 00:28:01,980
will be livestreamed on this channel!

528
00:28:02,547 --> 00:28:05,150
- Livestreamed?
- What the heck is going on?

529
00:28:05,216 --> 00:28:07,552
Okay, you guys. Let's do surgery.

530
00:28:07,619 --> 00:28:09,154
- Surgery?
- Us too?

531
00:28:15,794 --> 00:28:17,696
STREAMING MINISTER ENOMOTO'S OPERATION

532
00:28:17,762 --> 00:28:20,131
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL OFFICIAL CHANNEL

533
00:28:21,666 --> 00:28:24,736
There are already over 50,000 viewers.

534
00:28:26,638 --> 00:28:29,207
And the numbers will continue to climb.

535
00:28:30,475 --> 00:28:34,279
Since Minister Enomoto's
mild illness was revealed,

536
00:28:34,345 --> 00:28:36,514
he wants to avoid
destruction of his reputation.

537
00:28:36,581 --> 00:28:40,218
And Dr. Daimon wants to operate
on her patient.

538
00:28:40,285 --> 00:28:43,655
Our hospital wants to show the world
our capabilities.

539
00:28:43,722 --> 00:28:44,556
Right.

540
00:28:44,622 --> 00:28:49,327
Everyone, all these problems
can be fixed simultaneously.

541
00:28:50,662 --> 00:28:52,397
In other words…

542
00:28:54,132 --> 00:28:55,600
<i>Surgery on a substitute.</i>

543
00:28:57,035 --> 00:28:59,637
<i>Who would have thought</i>
<i>he would actually do this?</i>

544
00:29:00,705 --> 00:29:03,608
<i>That Chief Hachisuka</i>
<i>is actually pretty frightening.</i>

545
00:29:06,945 --> 00:29:11,249
Who would have thought we would broadcast
this old woman's surgery

546
00:29:11,316 --> 00:29:14,519
as if it were the surgery
of a government minister?

547
00:29:14,586 --> 00:29:16,888
And the surgeon is…

548
00:29:22,127 --> 00:29:23,895
It's not Michiko Daimon?

549
00:29:25,997 --> 00:29:27,732
Our creator!

550
00:29:27,799 --> 00:29:29,467
Our Buddha!

551
00:29:29,534 --> 00:29:31,870
Our great Michiko Daimon!

552
00:29:35,707 --> 00:29:37,075
Vitals are stable.

553
00:29:38,276 --> 00:29:39,377
Okay.

554
00:29:42,514 --> 00:29:43,348
<i>Dr. Daimon,</i>

555
00:29:43,414 --> 00:29:46,117
thank you for doing Yasue's surgery.

556
00:29:46,184 --> 00:29:47,752
I'm not doing it.

557
00:29:47,819 --> 00:29:50,588
- What? Why not?
- That's her wish.

558
00:29:51,189 --> 00:29:53,057
What? Her wish?

559
00:29:53,124 --> 00:29:54,793
Do your best.

560
00:29:54,859 --> 00:29:56,294
"Do your best"?

561
00:29:56,928 --> 00:29:58,797
Patient coming through.

562
00:30:04,269 --> 00:30:05,937
What's going on, Yasue?

563
00:30:06,004 --> 00:30:10,475
Mom said that if you'll operate,
then she'll have the surgery.

564
00:30:10,542 --> 00:30:12,911
I want you to do the surgery.

565
00:30:12,977 --> 00:30:14,646
I know you can do it.

566
00:30:16,014 --> 00:30:19,851
Of all people, she chose you to do it.

567
00:30:21,286 --> 00:30:24,756
Well, you'll just have
to buck up and go for it.

568
00:30:34,699 --> 00:30:37,268
- Are you all right?
- Yes.

569
00:30:38,770 --> 00:30:42,707
We will now conduct a pyloric resection.

570
00:30:42,774 --> 00:30:43,741
- Scalpel.
- Here.

571
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:56,588
STREAMING MINISTER ENOMOTO'S OPERATION

572
00:30:56,654 --> 00:30:59,724
- It's being livestreamed?
- This is amazing!

573
00:30:59,791 --> 00:31:01,025
Bovie.

574
00:31:04,529 --> 00:31:06,097
MINISTER ENOMOTO'S OPERATION IS TRENDING

575
00:31:06,164 --> 00:31:08,867
Our video is one
of the top trending videos!

576
00:31:08,933 --> 00:31:10,969
All of Japan is watching!

577
00:31:12,470 --> 00:31:15,039
Will it be all right
without Michiko Daimon operating?

578
00:31:22,413 --> 00:31:23,481
Okay.

579
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:25,583
- Energy device.
- Here.

580
00:31:31,422 --> 00:31:33,291
Be careful. It hemorrhages easily.

581
00:31:34,225 --> 00:31:35,193
Right.

582
00:31:37,862 --> 00:31:39,163
- Sweat.
- Yes, sir.

583
00:31:39,230 --> 00:31:40,498
Already?

584
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:41,733
Thank you.

585
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:11,262
The tumor has penetrated
the tail of the pancreas.

586
00:32:12,397 --> 00:32:14,632
We'll need to resect the pancreas as well.

587
00:32:15,199 --> 00:32:16,200
What?

588
00:32:36,721 --> 00:32:37,956
Dr. Morimoto…

589
00:32:38,990 --> 00:32:42,226
You're expecting
the usual to happen, aren't you?

590
00:32:42,860 --> 00:32:43,695
What?

591
00:32:43,761 --> 00:32:45,229
Dr. Daimon is not coming.

592
00:32:46,230 --> 00:32:48,766
She was called away
to do another urgent surgery.

593
00:32:48,833 --> 00:32:49,667
Really?

594
00:32:49,734 --> 00:32:53,604
You have to complete
this surgery all on your own.

595
00:32:56,574 --> 00:32:57,408
Okay.

596
00:32:59,777 --> 00:33:01,713
I'll resect the tail of the pancreas.

597
00:33:04,482 --> 00:33:05,750
- Sweat.
- Yes, sir.

598
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:06,784
Again?

599
00:33:10,588 --> 00:33:12,490
Local anesthetic complete. Let's begin.

600
00:33:12,557 --> 00:33:14,859
I requested to be completely anesthetized!

601
00:33:14,926 --> 00:33:16,794
Don't whine. All the ORs are full.

602
00:33:16,861 --> 00:33:18,763
- I'm scared!
- The minister is scared.

603
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:21,366
- I'll finish this in a snap.
- Don't talk like that.

604
00:33:21,432 --> 00:33:23,134
- Let us know if it hurts.
- Okay.

605
00:33:23,201 --> 00:33:24,769
- It hurts!
- It does not!

606
00:33:24,836 --> 00:33:26,404
- I'm going to die!
- No, you won't!

607
00:33:26,471 --> 00:33:28,072
Quit overreacting!

608
00:33:28,139 --> 00:33:29,407
Hang in there!

609
00:33:29,474 --> 00:33:31,476
Don't move or you'll get a nosebleed!

610
00:33:31,542 --> 00:33:33,678
- Hang in there!
- Nice! There it is!

611
00:33:38,182 --> 00:33:40,485
SURGERY TIME

612
00:33:50,661 --> 00:33:53,364
Next, we'll resect the pylorus.
Linear stapler.

613
00:33:53,431 --> 00:33:54,332
Here.

614
00:33:59,871 --> 00:34:00,805
What's this?

615
00:34:04,308 --> 00:34:05,610
Peritoneal metastasis!

616
00:34:06,778 --> 00:34:07,912
You're kidding!

617
00:34:07,979 --> 00:34:10,281
What? Wait!

618
00:34:10,348 --> 00:34:11,783
Will this be all right?

619
00:34:12,283 --> 00:34:16,020
If this surgery is a failure,

620
00:34:16,087 --> 00:34:19,690
it will utterly ruin the reputation
of Totei University Hospital!

621
00:34:20,425 --> 00:34:22,160
It's metastasized to the omental bursa,

622
00:34:22,226 --> 00:34:23,694
so resection is impossible.

623
00:34:25,263 --> 00:34:26,230
It can't be removed.

624
00:34:26,297 --> 00:34:28,566
"Impossible"? You mean it has failed?

625
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:30,435
Dr. Morimoto…

626
00:34:32,503 --> 00:34:33,704
Let's close her up.

627
00:34:56,894 --> 00:34:58,229
We're closing.

628
00:34:59,263 --> 00:35:01,332
- 1-0 monofilament.
- Here.

629
00:35:20,151 --> 00:35:20,985
Dr. Daimon!

630
00:35:22,353 --> 00:35:23,821
Let me see.

631
00:35:23,888 --> 00:35:25,690
Things couldn't be worse.

632
00:35:26,491 --> 00:35:28,025
It's metastasized.

633
00:35:28,759 --> 00:35:30,661
Yes. Just as I expected.

634
00:35:31,329 --> 00:35:32,396
Right on time.

635
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:34,065
I'm taking over.

636
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:34,966
What?

637
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:36,734
I'm taking over!

638
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:38,336
What's going on?

639
00:35:38,402 --> 00:35:41,239
If this surgery is a failure,
what will happen to me?

640
00:35:41,305 --> 00:35:44,408
Since this is supposed to be
your surgery, then…

641
00:35:45,476 --> 00:35:47,211
you'll have to die.

642
00:35:48,212 --> 00:35:49,514
You've got to be kidding!

643
00:35:50,081 --> 00:35:52,283
Save me! Don't kill me!

644
00:35:53,384 --> 00:35:55,553
There's nothing more
to be done, Dr. Daimon.

645
00:35:56,687 --> 00:35:58,756
We'll remove the tumor via bursectomy.

646
00:35:59,757 --> 00:36:01,025
"Bursectomy"?

647
00:36:01,592 --> 00:36:04,128
Since the cancer has metastasized
to the omental bursa,

648
00:36:04,195 --> 00:36:06,130
it will be wrapped to prevent rupture,

649
00:36:06,197 --> 00:36:09,433
and the stomach, spleen,
and pancreas will be removed as one.

650
00:36:09,934 --> 00:36:12,203
It's impossible to wrap
and remove the omental bursa!

651
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:15,273
If it's forced out,
it could cause a pancreatic fistula!

652
00:36:20,311 --> 00:36:23,414
I will not fail.

653
00:36:26,684 --> 00:36:27,585
Oh, that's right.

654
00:36:30,121 --> 00:36:32,223
- Let's hurry. Linear stapler.
- Here.

655
00:36:33,424 --> 00:36:34,792
Don't just stand there.

656
00:36:34,859 --> 00:36:36,060
Yes, ma'am.

657
00:36:39,664 --> 00:36:40,831
- Bovie.
- Here.

658
00:36:41,399 --> 00:36:43,100
- Reduce to 8-8.
- Right.

659
00:36:43,668 --> 00:36:45,203
- Done.
- Okay.

660
00:36:53,077 --> 00:36:55,179
Ablating anterior lobe
of transverse colon.

661
00:36:55,246 --> 00:36:56,447
- Metz.
- Here.

662
00:36:56,981 --> 00:36:58,649
The omental bursa is fragile.

663
00:36:58,716 --> 00:37:00,384
Be careful opening the site.

664
00:37:00,451 --> 00:37:01,352
Got it.

665
00:37:12,763 --> 00:37:13,864
Gently.

666
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,635
Resection complete.

667
00:37:17,702 --> 00:37:18,669
Time to reconstruct.

668
00:37:18,736 --> 00:37:19,837
- Bovie.
- Here.

669
00:37:42,827 --> 00:37:46,264
BP 120 over 80, pulse 80, normal sinus.

670
00:37:47,164 --> 00:37:48,099
We're done.

671
00:37:48,165 --> 00:37:49,700
- Nice work.
- Well done.

672
00:38:22,633 --> 00:38:23,534
Mom?

673
00:38:27,271 --> 00:38:30,341
The surgery was a success.

674
00:38:31,042 --> 00:38:35,413
Dr. Morimoto removed the cancer.

675
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:37,348
I see…

676
00:38:39,016 --> 00:38:40,851
How can I thank you?

677
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:46,257
You're wrong.

678
00:38:49,660 --> 00:38:50,761
The truth is…

679
00:38:51,929 --> 00:38:53,331
it wasn't me.

680
00:38:55,700 --> 00:38:57,802
The removal of the tumor
was too difficult.

681
00:38:59,203 --> 00:39:01,672
I relied on the skills of a super doctor

682
00:39:01,739 --> 00:39:04,108
whose ability
I cannot even imagine matching.

683
00:39:05,176 --> 00:39:06,243
I…

684
00:39:07,845 --> 00:39:09,046
I…

685
00:39:12,616 --> 00:39:17,188
You're exactly the kind of person
I've always thought you were.

686
00:39:18,823 --> 00:39:23,294
You're sincere, honest, and upright.

687
00:39:24,962 --> 00:39:28,933
That's why the super doctor helped you.

688
00:39:33,270 --> 00:39:34,572
Dr. Morimoto…

689
00:39:36,307 --> 00:39:37,842
Thank you.

690
00:39:53,090 --> 00:39:54,458
Dr. Daimon!

691
00:39:57,528 --> 00:39:59,230
Thank you!

692
00:39:59,897 --> 00:40:01,899
Thanks to you, I realized…

693
00:40:02,666 --> 00:40:06,937
the real job of a doctor is to deal
with each patient individually.

694
00:40:07,571 --> 00:40:10,474
I'll return to my father's clinic
and try again.

695
00:40:10,541 --> 00:40:13,277
I'll work with each patient properly.

696
00:40:13,344 --> 00:40:14,945
You probably shouldn't.

697
00:40:15,679 --> 00:40:16,514
What?

698
00:40:16,580 --> 00:40:18,616
I mean, you're an awful surgeon.

699
00:40:18,682 --> 00:40:21,452
The only good thing about you is…

700
00:40:22,987 --> 00:40:24,822
that you're honest to a fault.

701
00:40:28,626 --> 00:40:30,494
Thank you!

702
00:40:31,862 --> 00:40:33,531
What's his problem?

703
00:40:37,568 --> 00:40:41,839
Minister Enomoto's cancer
was magnificently removed!

704
00:40:43,007 --> 00:40:44,041
However,

705
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:46,510
if the cancer had been detected earlier,

706
00:40:46,577 --> 00:40:49,513
it could have been cured
without operating,

707
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:53,250
using our hospital's chemical surgery.

708
00:40:53,317 --> 00:40:56,487
Unfortunately, we were unable to do that.

709
00:40:57,788 --> 00:41:00,825
The internal medicine style of treatment

710
00:41:00,891 --> 00:41:03,694
at Totei University Hospital
is extremely advanced.

711
00:41:03,761 --> 00:41:08,065
It is revolutionary, cutting-edge,
as well as ecological.

712
00:41:08,666 --> 00:41:10,668
There he goes, tooting his own horn.

713
00:41:10,734 --> 00:41:13,437
To acknowledge this new style,

714
00:41:13,504 --> 00:41:15,639
I would like to grant…

715
00:41:16,407 --> 00:41:20,311
Totei University Hospital
Green Ecology certification.

716
00:41:20,878 --> 00:41:22,546
Thank you!

717
00:41:23,214 --> 00:41:24,415
Then…

718
00:41:25,115 --> 00:41:27,651
Acting Director Hiruma,
please give a closing comment.

719
00:41:27,718 --> 00:41:29,753
You want me to?

720
00:41:29,820 --> 00:41:33,691
This surgery was only made possible
through…

721
00:41:33,757 --> 00:41:36,494
your strenuous efforts,
Acting Director Hiruma.

722
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:39,897
Oh, hardly. But thank you.

723
00:41:39,964 --> 00:41:43,834
I am Acting Director Hiruma.
It's nice to speak to you.

724
00:41:43,901 --> 00:41:46,837
Allow me to express my thanks to you.

725
00:41:46,904 --> 00:41:49,507
Thank you so much.

726
00:41:49,573 --> 00:41:51,108
Congratulations!

727
00:42:00,351 --> 00:42:02,419
SHICHIMIYA DINER

728
00:42:02,486 --> 00:42:03,888
This is a melon.

729
00:42:07,291 --> 00:42:08,726
This is a contract.

730
00:42:09,293 --> 00:42:11,595
A contract? Not a bill?

731
00:42:11,662 --> 00:42:16,233
The bill for this surgery
went to Chief Hachisuka.

732
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:20,271
Acting Director Hiruma
was merely a figurehead this time.

733
00:42:21,839 --> 00:42:22,873
But what's this?

734
00:42:22,940 --> 00:42:25,910
I'm taking this opportunity to restart

735
00:42:26,477 --> 00:42:30,047
Kambara Famous Doctor Agency
as Kambara Famous Doctor

736
00:42:30,114 --> 00:42:32,650
and Famous ExTuber Agency.

737
00:42:34,418 --> 00:42:37,154
As for our fees…

738
00:42:37,221 --> 00:42:41,091
I've decided to quit being an ExTuber.

739
00:42:41,158 --> 00:42:42,626
- You're quitting?
- Yes.

740
00:42:43,627 --> 00:42:47,498
What I want isn't money or popularity.

741
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:51,435
I realized I want pride
and confidence as a doctor.

742
00:42:52,436 --> 00:42:54,805
- I see…
- I'm sorry.

743
00:42:56,273 --> 00:42:57,942
You are really a fool.

744
00:42:58,008 --> 00:43:00,344
But that's why I like you.

745
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:01,312
Voilà!

746
00:43:01,378 --> 00:43:02,846
The Dr. Morimoto special!

747
00:43:02,913 --> 00:43:04,915
Oh, wow! That's awesome!

748
00:43:05,549 --> 00:43:07,518
We'll be rooting for you!

749
00:43:08,018 --> 00:43:08,986
Thank you.

750
00:43:09,053 --> 00:43:11,221
By the way, where's Dr. Daimon?

751
00:43:17,361 --> 00:43:18,896
<i>She hates groups,</i>

752
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:20,397
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

753
00:43:20,464 --> 00:43:22,333
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

754
00:43:23,467 --> 00:43:26,637
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

755
00:43:26,704 --> 00:43:28,205
<i>to work her way up.</i>

756
00:43:33,243 --> 00:43:36,413
Thank you for accepting
my sudden invitation.

757
00:43:36,981 --> 00:43:38,449
I appreciate it.

758
00:43:38,515 --> 00:43:40,818
Lately, my chef has been slacking off.

759
00:43:42,886 --> 00:43:43,887
This meat…

760
00:43:43,954 --> 00:43:46,223
This meat is so delicious!

761
00:43:46,290 --> 00:43:47,124
I'm glad you like it.

762
00:43:47,758 --> 00:43:49,493
You handle your knife beautifully.

763
00:43:50,294 --> 00:43:51,795
The vegetables are delicious too.

764
00:44:04,908 --> 00:44:06,644
Somewhere in this world,

765
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:11,181
there is a legendary doctor
called Doctor X.

766
00:44:11,915 --> 00:44:14,785
If they really do exist,

767
00:44:15,786 --> 00:44:18,155
I would like to speak with them

768
00:44:18,222 --> 00:44:19,890
about the future of medicine.

769
00:44:21,892 --> 00:44:23,193
That was delicious.

770
00:44:24,528 --> 00:44:26,030
Thanks for the meal, Dr. Hachisuka.

771
00:44:33,904 --> 00:44:35,072
Whoa!

772
00:44:36,740 --> 00:44:38,375
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

773
00:44:38,442 --> 00:44:39,276
Thank you.

774
00:44:43,847 --> 00:44:47,451
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

775
00:44:50,154 --> 00:44:52,256
You haven't changed a single bit.

776
00:44:52,322 --> 00:44:54,658
<i>I know very well</i>
<i>that I don't have much longer.</i>

777
00:44:54,725 --> 00:44:55,759
Let me operate on you.

778
00:44:55,826 --> 00:44:57,828
This patient can't be operated on.

779
00:44:57,895 --> 00:44:59,730
Do you always want to be
Hachisuka's jerk's dog?

780
00:44:59,797 --> 00:45:01,065
I think this is fate.

781
00:45:01,131 --> 00:45:02,833
I told you I don't give up easily.

782
00:45:02,900 --> 00:45:03,867
Satsuki!

783
00:45:03,934 --> 00:45:05,302
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
